CM_ BO_ 560 "Absolute DAC, shared midpoint, and relay command. DAC1_Code and DAC2_Code are raw 12-bit DAC codes. Midpoint_InputVoltage is the external input voltage before halving for the DAC center; SaveToNVM stores that midpoint to flash.";
CM_ BO_ 561 "Differential DAC command matching terminal SET/DAC behavior. DAC_Delta and DAC_Delta_Redundant are signed little-endian and must match, byte4 carries relay commands plus openpilot limit-hit bits including OP_OutTq, Delta_Counter is a 4-bit rolling counter in byte5 bits0..3 that is sequence-checked modulo 16 after the first valid frame, and Delta_Checksum is CRC-8 over id_lo, id_hi, and bytes0..5 with polynomial 0x07 and init 0x00.";
CM_ BO_ 562 "Desired EPS output torque command. Torque_Demand uses the low 12 bits of bytes0..1 as a signed Ncm output-torque demand, Torque_Demand_Complement carries the 12-bit ones-complement of that raw field in bytes2..3, byte4 carries relay commands plus openpilot limit-hit bits including OP_OutTq, Torque_Counter is a 4-bit rolling counter in byte5 bits0..3 that is sequence-checked modulo 16 across accepted 0x232 frames, and Torque_Checksum is CRC-8 over id_lo, id_hi, and bytes0..5 with polynomial 0x07 and init 0x00. The receiver requires recent forwarded 0x1F1 wheel speed, maps desired output torque to required MDPS input torque with a speed-binned drive-log map, then applies the torque-to-DAC calibration. It rejects stale speed, implausible torque jumps, and large sign flips away from zero; demands above +-801 Ncm are clipped to +-801 Ncm and reported with Output_Range_Error.";
CM_ BO_ 576 "ADC1..ADC5 raw 12-bit conversion codes packed into 8 bytes; bits60..62 report SNR passthrough requested, active, and torque-confirm-pending state; bit63 is currently unused.";
CM_ BO_ 577 "Reported DAC output codes packed as two 12-bit fields, EPS_VREF as a 12-bit field at 1.25 mV/LSB, relay and RC input states, TRQI delta-command error flags, watchdog timeout state, a 4-bit IOStatus_Counter, SNR/EPS pair plausibility error bits, Delta_Counter_Error, Output_Range_Error, local DAC feedback and RC state error bits, live torque-calibration state bits, and IOStatus_Checksum. RC_Minus maps PB4, RC_Plus maps PB1.";
CM_ BO_ 578 "Expanded TRQI fault and limiter detail. Byte0 carries disengage/report-only error summary, limit summary, safe-state, CAN category, and pending-delay bits; bytes1..3 carry individual error bits; bytes4..5 carry individual limiter bits; byte6 is FaultStatus_Counter; byte7 is CRC-8 over id_lo, id_hi, and bytes0..6 with polynomial 0x07 and init 0x00. Command/diagnostic event details latch until the next valid command; CAN transport event details remain visible during the transient hold window; live diagnostic bits also reflect active status.";
CM_ BO_ 579 "SNR1/SNR2/EPS1/EPS2 input voltages after divider scaling, sent as packed 12-bit values at 1.25 mV/LSB (0..5.11875 V), followed by VoltageStatus_Counter and VoltageStatus_Checksum.";
CM_ BO_ 580 "Latest accepted 0x232 torque-map calculation for debugging. Reports the vehicle speed used, limited EPS output-torque demand, mapped MDPS input torque, speed-bin interpolation indexes, torque-axis point index, and map coverage/extrapolation flags. The frame has no checksum or counter; MapDebug_Valid is cleared outside active torque-map control.";

CM_ SG_ 560 DAC1_Code "Raw 12-bit DAC code 0..4095. DAC1 is the project DAC1 label mapped to PA5 / DAC_CHANNEL_2; about 2048 is midscale in the 0..5 V domain.";
CM_ SG_ 560 DAC2_Code "Raw 12-bit DAC code 0..4095. DAC2 is the project DAC2 label mapped to PA4 / DAC_CHANNEL_1; about 2048 is midscale in the 0..5 V domain.";
CM_ SG_ 561 DAC_Delta "Signed raw DAC-count offset around the active midpoint; this is in code counts, not volts.";
CM_ SG_ 561 DAC_Delta_Redundant "Redundant copy of DAC_Delta; it must match DAC_Delta exactly for the command to be accepted.";
CM_ SG_ 561 Delta_Counter "4-bit rolling counter carried in byte5 bits0..3 for 0x231; after the first valid delta frame the receiver expects the next modulo-16 value.";
CM_ SG_ 562 Torque_Demand "Signed desired EPS output torque demand in Ncm carried in the low 12 bits of bytes0..1. Accepted 0x232 frames are mapped through recent 0x1F1 speed into required MDPS input torque, then converted through the built-in or live torque-to-DAC calibration into absolute DAC1/DAC2 outputs.";
CM_ SG_ 562 Torque_Demand_Complement "12-bit ones-complement redundancy for Torque_Demand. It is encoded as Torque_Demand raw12 XOR 0x0FFF in the low 12 bits of bytes2..3.";
CM_ SG_ 562 OP_Steer_Delta_Up_Limited "Set by openpilot when the TRQI torque command was clipped by the openpilot STEER_DELTA_UP limit before transmission.";
CM_ SG_ 562 OP_Steer_Delta_Down_Limited "Set by openpilot when the TRQI torque command was clipped by the openpilot STEER_DELTA_DOWN limit before transmission.";
CM_ SG_ 562 OP_Steer_Max_Limited "Set by openpilot when the TRQI torque command was clipped by the openpilot STEER_MAX/MAX_STEERING_TQ limit before transmission.";
CM_ SG_ 562 OP_OutTq_Limited "Set by openpilot while measured VSM2.CR_Mdps_OutTq exceeds the configured threshold.";
CM_ SG_ 562 Torque_Counter "4-bit rolling counter carried in byte5 bits0..3 for 0x232; after the first valid torque frame the receiver expects the next modulo-16 value.";
CM_ SG_ 562 Torque_Checksum "8-bit CRC of the 0x232 message over id_lo, id_hi, and bytes0..5 using polynomial 0x07 and init 0x00.";
CM_ SG_ 576 ADC1_Raw "Raw 12-bit ADC conversion code 0..4095 from PB15 / SNR1 before divider scaling to input volts.";
CM_ SG_ 576 ADC2_Raw "Raw 12-bit ADC conversion code 0..4095 from PB13 / SNR2 before divider scaling to input volts.";
CM_ SG_ 576 ADC3_Raw "Raw 12-bit ADC conversion code 0..4095 from PA1 / EPS1 before divider scaling to input volts.";
CM_ SG_ 576 ADC4_Raw "Raw 12-bit ADC conversion code 0..4095 from PA2 / EPS2 before divider scaling to input volts.";
CM_ SG_ 576 ADC5_Raw "Raw 12-bit ADC conversion code 0..4095 from PA8 / EPS_VREF before divider scaling to input volts.";
CM_ SG_ 577 SNR_Pair_Error "Set when the SNR pair differs by more than the configured plausibility bound in distance from EPS_VREF/2, or when both SNR signals move to the same side of EPS_VREF/2 once meaningfully away from center. Starts the diagnostic safe-state delay.";
CM_ SG_ 577 EPS_Pair_Error "Set when the EPS pair differs by more than the configured plausibility bound in distance from EPS_VREF/2, or when both EPS signals move to the same side of EPS_VREF/2 once meaningfully away from center. Starts the diagnostic safe-state delay.";
CM_ SG_ 577 DAC1_Code "Reported raw 12-bit DAC code 0..4095. DAC1 is the project DAC1 label mapped to PA5 / DAC_CHANNEL_2; about 2048 is midscale in the 0..5 V domain.";
CM_ SG_ 577 DAC2_Code "Reported raw 12-bit DAC code 0..4095. DAC2 is the project DAC2 label mapped to PA4 / DAC_CHANNEL_1; about 2048 is midscale in the 0..5 V domain.";
CM_ SG_ 560 SaveToNVM "When set, the midpoint value is saved to internal flash.";
CM_ SG_ 561 OP_Steer_Delta_Up_Limited "Set by openpilot when the TRQI command was clipped by the openpilot STEER_DELTA_UP limit before transmission.";
CM_ SG_ 561 OP_Steer_Delta_Down_Limited "Set by openpilot when the TRQI command was clipped by the openpilot STEER_DELTA_DOWN limit before transmission.";
CM_ SG_ 561 OP_Steer_Max_Limited "Set by openpilot when the TRQI command was clipped by the openpilot STEER_MAX/MAX_STEERING_TQ limit before transmission.";
CM_ SG_ 561 OP_OutTq_Limited "Set by openpilot while measured VSM2.CR_Mdps_OutTq exceeds the configured threshold.";
CM_ SG_ 561 Delta_Checksum "8-bit CRC of the 0x231 message over id_lo, id_hi, and bytes0..5 using polynomial 0x07 and init 0x00.";
CM_ SG_ 577 RC_Minus "Digital input PB4 / RC-.";
CM_ SG_ 577 RC_Plus "Digital input PB1 / RC+.";
CM_ SG_ 577 Delta_Dlc_Error "Set when the last TRQI delta frame was rejected because DLC was shorter than 7 bytes.";
CM_ SG_ 577 Delta_Mismatch_Error "Set when the last TRQI delta frame was rejected because DAC_Delta and DAC_Delta_Redundant did not match.";
CM_ SG_ 577 Delta_Checksum_Error "Set when the last TRQI delta frame was rejected because Delta_Checksum did not match the computed CRC-8 value.";
CM_ SG_ 577 CAN_WDG_TIMO "Set when the TRQI command watchdog timed out after 500 ms without a valid 0x230, 0x231, or 0x232 command; outputs are forced to neutral center and both relays are driven off.";
CM_ SG_ 577 Delta_Counter_Error "Set when the last TRQI delta frame was rejected because Delta_Counter was not the expected next modulo-16 value; the receiver resynchronizes to the received counter.";
CM_ SG_ 577 IOStatus_Counter "4-bit rolling counter incremented on each successful 0x241 transmit.";
CM_ SG_ 577 Output_Range_Error "Set when an absolute, delta, or torque TRQI command would drive DAC1 or DAC2 outside the allowed 1.2..3.5 V output window, or when a 0x232 output-torque demand exceeded +-801 Ncm, and the firmware had to clamp the output.";
CM_ SG_ 577 DAC_FB_Error "Set when the local CANCTR DAC feedback check is active because EPS1/EPS2 do not match the applied DAC outputs within the configured thresholds.";
CM_ SG_ 577 RC_State_Error "Set when the local CANCTR RC state check is active because PB4/PB1 do not match the expected relay-state combination.";
CM_ SG_ 577 TorqueCal_Valid "Set when a live PC4 torque calibration has completed successfully and its RAM map is valid.";
CM_ SG_ 577 TorqueCal_Active "Set while a live PC4 torque calibration capture is currently running.";
CM_ SG_ 577 IOStatus_Checksum "8-bit CRC of the 0x241 message over id_lo, id_hi, and bytes0..6 using polynomial 0x07 and init 0x00.";
CM_ SG_ 578 Disengage_Error "Set when any active individual error bit is in the disengage-class mask. Current TRQI error bits are disengage-class; limit bits are reported separately through Any_Limit.";
CM_ SG_ 578 Any_Limit "Set when any individual limiter bit in TRQI_FaultStatus is active.";
CM_ SG_ 578 Diagnostic_Safe_State_Pending "Set while a confirmed DAC feedback, RC state, SNR pair, or EPS pair error is waiting for the 100 ms diagnostic safe-state delay to expire.";
CM_ SG_ 578 CAN_Error_Disengage_Pending "Set while a CAN controller/RX/TX/overrun fault is waiting for the 100 ms CAN error disengage delay to expire.";
CM_ SG_ 578 Transient_Error_Hold "Set while the local transient error hold is active for LED/diagnostic visibility.";
CM_ SG_ 578 Commanded_Safe_State "Set when the latest valid 0x230/0x231/0x232 control command requested safe state by not commanding both REL and RELE; clears on the next valid active command or mode reset.";
CM_ SG_ 578 CAN_Error "Set when any CAN transport/controller detail bit is active.";
CM_ SG_ 578 Non_Disengage_Error "Set when any active individual error bit is report-only and does not request safe state. No current TRQI error bits are in this class.";
CM_ SG_ 578 Watchdog_Timeout_Error "Set when the 500 ms CANCTR command watchdog has timed out.";
CM_ SG_ 578 Abs_Dlc_Error "Set when a 0x230 absolute command was shorter than the required 7 bytes.";
CM_ SG_ 578 Abs_Mode_Error "Set when a 0x230 absolute command was rejected because torque mode was active.";
CM_ SG_ 578 Delta_Dlc_Error_Detail "Set when a 0x231 delta command was shorter than the required 7 bytes.";
CM_ SG_ 578 Delta_Mismatch_Error_Detail "Set when a 0x231 delta command redundant delta did not match the primary delta.";
CM_ SG_ 578 Delta_Checksum_Error_Detail "Set when a 0x231 delta command checksum failed.";
CM_ SG_ 578 Delta_Counter_Error_Detail "Set when a 0x231 delta command counter was repeated, too old, or skipped farther than the allowed tolerance.";
CM_ SG_ 578 Delta_Mode_Error "Set when a 0x231 delta command was rejected because torque mode was active.";
CM_ SG_ 578 Torque_Dlc_Error "Set when a 0x232 torque command was shorter than the required 7 bytes.";
CM_ SG_ 578 Torque_Checksum_Error "Set when a 0x232 torque command checksum failed.";
CM_ SG_ 578 Torque_Complement_Error "Set when a 0x232 torque command 12-bit complement did not match Torque_Demand.";
CM_ SG_ 578 Torque_Counter_Error "Set when a 0x232 torque command counter was repeated, too old, or skipped farther than the allowed tolerance.";
CM_ SG_ 578 Torque_Stale_Speed_Error "Set when a 0x232 torque command was rejected because no recent forwarded 0x1F1 wheel speed was available.";
CM_ SG_ 578 Torque_Sign_Flip_Error "Set when a 0x232 torque command was rejected for a large sign flip away from zero.";
CM_ SG_ 578 Torque_Step_Error "Set when a 0x232 torque command was rejected for exceeding the allowed torque step/rate guard.";
CM_ SG_ 578 SNR_Pair_Error_Detail "Set when the SNR pair plausibility check is active, or latched as the cause of a diagnostic safe-state transition.";
CM_ SG_ 578 EPS_Pair_Error_Detail "Set when the EPS pair plausibility check is active, or latched as the cause of a diagnostic safe-state transition.";
CM_ SG_ 578 DAC_FB_Error_Detail "Set when the DAC feedback check is active, or latched as the cause of a diagnostic safe-state transition.";
CM_ SG_ 578 RC_State_Error_Detail "Set when the RC state check is active, or latched as the cause of a diagnostic safe-state transition.";
CM_ SG_ 578 CAN_RX_FIFO_Lost_Error "Set when FDCAN reports an RX FIFO0 message-lost event while CANCTR is active.";
CM_ SG_ 578 CAN_Controller_Error "Set when FDCAN reports a controller/protocol status interrupt while CANCTR is active.";
CM_ SG_ 578 CAN_TX_Drop_Error "Set when a CANCTR status frame could not be queued after retries.";
CM_ SG_ 578 CAN_RX_Overrun_Error "Set when a latest-frame slot was overwritten before the CANCTR frame was processed, or when the local CAN RX queue overflowed and dropped frames.";
CM_ SG_ 578 DAC_Output_Clamp_Limit "Set when CANCTR clamps DAC1 or DAC2 to the allowed 1.2..3.5 V output window.";
CM_ SG_ 578 Torque_Demand_Clamp_Limit "Set when a 0x232 output torque demand exceeded +-801 Ncm and was clipped.";
CM_ SG_ 578 Delta_Demand_Clamp_Limit "Set when a 0x231 delta command exceeded the raw DAC delta range and was clipped.";
CM_ SG_ 578 Abs_DAC_Code_Clamp_Limit "Set when a 0x230 absolute DAC code exceeded the raw 12-bit DAC range and was clipped.";
CM_ SG_ 578 Abs_Midpoint_Clamp_Limit "Set when a 0x230 midpoint input implied an output midpoint above the 0..5 V DAC domain and was clipped.";
CM_ SG_ 578 OP_Steer_Delta_Up_Limit "Mirrors the latest valid 0x231/0x232 OP_STEER_DELTA_UP limiter flag from the command source.";
CM_ SG_ 578 OP_Steer_Delta_Down_Limit "Mirrors the latest valid 0x231/0x232 OP_STEER_DELTA_DOWN limiter flag from the command source.";
CM_ SG_ 578 OP_Steer_Max_Limit "Mirrors the latest valid 0x231/0x232 OP_STEER_MAX limiter flag from the command source.";
CM_ SG_ 578 OP_OutTq_Limit "Mirrors the latest valid 0x231/0x232 OP_OUTTQ limiter flag from the command source.";
CM_ SG_ 578 FaultStatus_Counter "8-bit counter incremented on each successful 0x242 transmit.";
CM_ SG_ 578 FaultStatus_Checksum "8-bit CRC of the 0x242 message over id_lo, id_hi, and bytes0..6 using polynomial 0x07 and init 0x00.";
CM_ SG_ 576 SNR_Passthrough_Requested "Set when SNR passthrough is requested by the SNR1/SNR2 difference threshold and has not released yet.";
CM_ SG_ 576 SNR_Passthrough_Active "Set while SNR passthrough is blended into the applied DAC output.";
CM_ SG_ 576 SNR_Passthrough_Pending "Set while torque-mode SNR passthrough is waiting for the short anti-spike confirmation window.";
CM_ SG_ 579 VoltageStatus_Counter "8-bit rolling counter incremented on each successful 0x243 transmit.";
CM_ SG_ 579 VoltageStatus_Checksum "8-bit CRC of the 0x243 message over id_lo, id_hi, and bytes0..6 using polynomial 0x07 and init 0x00.";
CM_ SG_ 580 MapDebug_Speed "Vehicle speed used by the latest accepted 0x232 torque-map calculation.";
CM_ SG_ 580 MapDebug_OutputTorque "Limited EPS output torque demand passed into the speed map.";
CM_ SG_ 580 MapDebug_InputTorque "MDPS input torque produced by the speed map before torque-to-DAC conversion.";
CM_ SG_ 580 MapDebug_SpeedBin_Lower "Lower speed-bin row index used for interpolation; equals MapDebug_SpeedBin_Upper when speed is outside or exactly on an endpoint row.";
CM_ SG_ 580 MapDebug_SpeedBin_Upper "Upper speed-bin row index used for interpolation; equals MapDebug_SpeedBin_Lower when speed is outside or exactly on an endpoint row.";
CM_ SG_ 580 MapDebug_Valid "Set when the frame contains a current accepted 0x232 torque-map sample; cleared after safe state, absolute/delta control, or mode reset.";
CM_ SG_ 580 MapDebug_Torque_Clipped "Set when the original 0x232 output torque demand was clipped to +-801 Ncm before mapping.";
CM_ SG_ 580 MapDebug_TorquePoint_Upper "Upper output-torque point index used on the map torque axis. For endpoint extrapolation this is the endpoint index.";
CM_ SG_ 580 MapDebug_Torque_Extrapolated "Set when the limited output torque is outside the generated map torque-axis range.";
CM_ SG_ 580 MapDebug_Speed_Extrapolated "Set when speed is outside the generated speed-bin center range and the endpoint speed row is used.";
CM_ SG_ 580 MapDebug_Cell_Calibrated "Set when all speed/torque map cells used by the current interpolation are marked calibrated in the generated map.";

